@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Existing endpoint; change learning.message through configuration.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/learning/status

### 2. Create a product. Save its returned ID for the next requests.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Mechanical keyboard","price":1250.00,"stock":10}

> {% client.global.set("productId", response.body.id); %}

### 3. Read the product (also repeat after restarting the application).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}

### 4. Invalid input: expect 400 and fieldErrors.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"","price":-1,"stock":-1}

### 5. Dirty checking: change price, then repeat request 3.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}/price
Content-Type: application/json

{"price":1199.00}

### 6. Create an order: expect total 2398.00 and product stock 8.
# These expectations assume a fresh product and one run of requests 5 and 6.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"productId":{{productId}},"quantity":2}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id); %}

### 7. Read the order.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}

### 8. Insufficient stock: expect 409; repeat request 3 to inspect unchanged stock.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"productId":{{productId}},"quantity":100}

### 9. Missing resource: expect 404.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/9223372036854775807
